{"sourceSha256": "15d8af8f9251ddf7356baa27eae9d6ca8edfa5e07c0cc5279567589cf4ceee8c", "text": "T-\\ T\noe E SPEAKING SUB-TEST\n\n| ROLE PLAYER'S CARD NO. 1 NURSING\n\nSETTING Maternity Ward\n\nPATIENT You are in hospital for delivery of your third child by Caesarean Section, when you are\nalso diagnosed with rheumatoid arthvitis. You have severe pain in your wrists and\nshoulders, and you are feeling very fatiqued, as the pain is disturbing your sleep, You are\nworried about using any medication while breastfeeding\n\nComplain to the nurse about your pain but insist on not taking any oral\nmedications for the pain or sleeping problems.\n\nExpress your fear that the medication may harm your baby and you are\ndetermined to breastfeed the baby\n\nFirmly insist on using a natural gel product which contains capsaicin anc is\nreputed to help with pain reliel. Be very agitated by the nurse's insistence on\nprescribed medication,\n\nAsk how soon you should expect to be able to go home\n\nCANDIDATE'S CARD NURSING\n\nSETTING = Maternity Ward\n\nNURSE This 41 year-old patient is in hospital for delivery of her third child by Caesarean Section,\nwhen she is also diagnosed with rheumatoid arthritis. She has severe pain in her wrists\nand shoulders and is feeling very fatigued, as the pain is disturbing her sleap. She is\nworried about breastfeeding whilst using any medications\n\nRespond sympathetically to the patient's demands and questions.\n\nExplain the reasons for the oral medication prescribed by her/ his doctor and try\nto persuade the patient to take this medication.\n\nReassure the patient of the safety of the oral medication. Try to calm the patient\ndown by suggesting other ways to also cope with the pain (hot/cold pack, arrange\nfor Inend/relative support, review by doctor).", "pages": [{"number": 1, "text": "T-\\ T\noe E SPEAKING SUB-TEST\n\n| ROLE PLAYER'S CARD NO. 1 NURSING\n\nSETTING Maternity Ward\n\nPATIENT You are in hospital for delivery of your third child by Caesarean Section, when you are\nalso diagnosed with rheumatoid arthvitis. You have severe pain in your wrists and\nshoulders, and you are feeling very fatiqued, as the pain is disturbing your sleep, You are\nworried about using any medication while breastfeeding\n\nComplain to the nurse about your pain but insist on not taking any oral\nmedications for the pain or sleeping problems.\n\nExpress your fear that the medication may harm your baby and you are\ndetermined to breastfeed the baby\n\nFirmly insist on using a natural gel product which contains capsaicin anc is\nreputed to help with pain reliel. Be very agitated by the nurse's insistence on\nprescribed medication,\n\nAsk how soon you should expect to be able to go home\n\nCANDIDATE'S CARD NURSING\n\nSETTING = Maternity Ward\n\nNURSE This 41 year-old patient is in hospital for delivery of her third child by Caesarean Section,\nwhen she is also diagnosed with rheumatoid arthritis. She has severe pain in her wrists\nand shoulders and is feeling very fatigued, as the pain is disturbing her sleap. She is\nworried about breastfeeding whilst using any medications\n\nRespond sympathetically to the patient's demands and questions.\n\nExplain the reasons for the oral medication prescribed by her/ his doctor and try\nto persuade the patient to take this medication.\n\nReassure the patient of the safety of the oral medication. Try to calm the patient\ndown by suggesting other ways to also cope with the pain (hot/cold pack, arrange\nfor Inend/relative support, review by doctor).", "extraction": "ocr", "layout": {"version": 1, "width": 1986.0, "height": 2800.0, "blocks": [{"text": "T-\\ T\noe E SPEAKING SUB-TEST", "lines": [{"text": "T-\\ T", "x": 0.16516, "y": 0.06107, "width": 0.10725, "height": 0.02857, "confidence": 0.429, "words": [{"text": "T-\\", "x": 0.16516, "width": 0.04028, "confidence": 0.0}, {"text": "T", "x": 0.23968, "width": 0.03273, "confidence": 0.859}], "uncertainWords": ["T-\\"]}, {"text": "oe E SPEAKIN